    "summary": "- `POST /v1/customers/import` parses the CSV, checks every record, and creates all customers or none. The store checks duplicate emails under one lock, so the import is atomic. Responses match the spec, and each created customer sends `customer.created` in file order.\n- `?dry_run=true` runs the same checks and returns `200 {\"created\":0,\"would_create\":N}` or the same 422, and creates nothing.\n- Tests in `internal/api/api_test.go` (`TestCustomerImport`) cover the header rules, CSV parsing, every row error code with its line number, the 10,000-row limit, atomicity, dry run, and events. `go build \n...[truncated]",
